  "comment": "Regression gate limits (tools/check_bench.py --baseline), Task 5c fix round 1. The bench carries the shipped application manifest, so every process runs on the Windows Segment Heap. Each of a side's 3 processes runs from its own copy of its build on one Windows runner; a process's time is Zodiac's ns over its machine-speed factor, the add-on side's median over operations against the processes of its own side only (so a slower head build is never divided away). Per operation the gate compares head's best process with main's median process; the geometric mean compares best with best. Data: 80 gate-replica A/A' jobs on the Segment Heap (two builds of one commit, the gate's exact runs): 45563519272, 45563526161, 45563532292, 45563538333, 45563543807 (c95a9e9) and 45568138113, 45568144279, 45568149503, 45568155630, 45568161908 (024033e); EPYC 7763 40, EPYC 9V74 13, EPYC 9V45 12, Xeon 8573C 8, Xeon 6973P-C 5, Xeon 8370C 2. An A/A' job is symmetric in its labels, so each gives two samples of the per-operation statistic (head best over main median, and main best over head median): 160 per operation. Rule, for x = ln(statistic): limit = exp(median(x) + 3.540 * 1.4826 * MAD(x) * b), b = sqrt(n / chi-square 5 % quantile with n degrees of freedom), rounded up to 0.01; never below the largest sample plus 1 % rounded up, and never below 1.03 (\"floor\": true where one of those two decides). The geometric mean's limit: exp(3.291 * s_upper), s the root mean square of its ln about 0. The model figure (0.02 % per operation and 0.05 % for the geometric mean, 0.99 % per run under a normal model of the bulk) is not a measurement: the samples are mirrored pairs, two per job from shared builds, the floors decide 10 operations, and a held-out job is near the data by construction. What the data supports: held out one job at a time, the limits from the other 79 failed none of the 80 jobs, and the 24 validation replicas run with this file (gate-replica 45572454201, 45572459584, 45572465905 at f0f766d, not used in the derivation) failed none: 0 false failures in 104 gate runs, a 95 % upper bound of about 2.9 % per run (3/104). An operation not listed takes the default 1.10 until gate-replica samples set its own.",
